066169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c6eb81a-1cc9-5429-bd9a-cd0c2b0e347a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439437} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e0f3ecf-3cbb-5900-9aa4-6c914b346e91" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440076}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "046b8096-a4b3-5639-81fd-05cfaf3fcc14" :question/math-academy-id "q-113527" :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-12}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-6$\n- **II.** $x=0$\n- **III.** $x=2$\n- **IV.** $x=6$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-12} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{{x}^{2}(x-2)+6(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{({x}^{2}+6)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+6)(x-2)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $x-2=0$ gives the solution $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+6=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Vertical Asymptotes With Common Factors When the Denominator Has Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b695010-193a-5cbf-8437-deaea37d1e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439445} {:answer/id #uuid "c3eb42b0-64fa-57df-989d-34ad71b77544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b695010-193a-5cbf-8437-deaea37d1e6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439445} :answer-field/id #uuid "a05fb1c2-71ab-5897-b477-b35b2b52f361" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440080} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07352cca-ef41-500b-abb4-1723978e1d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439447} {:answer/id #uuid "b86e32e1-d38b-5979-9b96-72ba9376f584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07352cca-ef41-500b-abb4-1723978e1d79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439447} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bab6831-3422-5ec6-825e-7496bd51fcff" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a883da7c-a136-5cbf-9a7a-a47b5396a663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439449} {:answer/id #uuid "ef060659-9b12-59fd-894d-bae2fed93853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a883da7c-a136-5cbf-9a7a-a47b5396a663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439449} :answer-field/id #uuid "a280265d-1249-5f5f-8a87-e044b6bc33ae" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60ce65c6-c9ad-50c2-b008-fca69d6b6025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439451} {:answer/id #uuid "0e3a6b46-9a94-5ba3-bf13-cf894946a7b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ce65c6-c9ad-50c2-b008-fca69d6b6025" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439451} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a35fdf6-4ccf-52f4-a7be-125347104920" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0085fda-c140-5022-a903-4aa2d0060987" :question/math-academy-id "q-113554" :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}-6}{{x}^{4}-9}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-3$\n- **II.** $x=- \\sqrt{3}$\n- **III.** $x=0$\n- **IV.** $x=\\sqrt{3}$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}-6}{{x}^{4}-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({x}^{2}-3)}{({x}^{2}-3)({x}^{2}+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cancel{({x}^{2}-3)}}{\\cancel{({x}^{2}-3)}({x}^{2}+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+3=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae4f142e-64ca-5cf1-bba5-1bb7e5f38aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439465} {:answer/id #uuid "de3a62f1-ef79-57d9-abd6-9050be028873" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae4f142e-64ca-5cf1-bba5-1bb7e5f38aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439465} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3764177-45a2-558b-9c90-1ce74f89c430" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440090} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df688db8-1580-5d94-85cf-dbb0c6d9127f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439467} {:answer/id #uuid "1ae03a63-04c8-5456-b96a-9013a1f5b82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ae03a63-