d/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440111} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa7553f1-861f-51c0-8547-71189b4ae228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439509} {:answer/id #uuid "3f812865-94f7-5778-aa60-73b89c449256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa7553f1-861f-51c0-8547-71189b4ae228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439509} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dd2c2d4-80d6-5681-8a2f-d724cd733e7a" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440112}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a633d445-62c8-5864-b7bf-d694cd1cd56c" :question/math-academy-id "q-128519" :question/problem "Given that $g(x,y)=\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x,$ find the points $(x,y)$ where $∇g(x,y)=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-3,-3)$\n- **II.** $(-3,3)$\n- **III.** $(3,-3)$\n- **IV.** $(3,3)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{9}{y}-\\frac{3y}{x}+x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{3}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇g(x,y)=(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1)i-(\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x})j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇g(x,y)=0:$\n\n$$\n(\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1)i-(\\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x})j=0\\,i+0\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}\\frac{3y}{{x}^{2}}+1=0 \\\\ \\frac{9}{{y}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x}=0\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $y=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{{(-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})}^{2}}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ 9\\cdot {(-\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}})}^{2}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{81}{{x}^{4}}+\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{81+3{x}^{3}}{{x}^{4}} & =0 \\\\ 81+3{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =-27 \\\\ x & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-3,$ we get $y=-\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{3}=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $∇g(x,y)=0$ at the point: $(-3,-3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3f9a2e3-bee8-5b1b-b1c5-43ca27a9ee8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439511} {:answer/id #uuid "f628d092-8784-5d3d-b54f-458bd5beb768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3f9a2e3-bee8-5b1b-b1c5-43ca27a9ee8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439511} :answer-field/id #uuid "d87136b4-f54f-5a06-86b5-cf63e992b1d1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12fafdc0-e4b2-52e6-ae9c-99cc3b27a59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439513} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b5298a-472b-5545-8b69-e594bf8766ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4b5298a-472b-5545-8b69-e594bf8766ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439514} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d688553-f546-5705-b1b5-e8fa688d5ccc" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440114} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d89573c1-b7fc-57e0-b937-a941c611e3b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439515} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2526f8-dbfa-54f5-953e-68b316490ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a2526f8-dbfa-54f5-953e-68b316490ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439516} :answer-field/id #uuid "0da4e8cd-a37a-575d-b740-45d4e50ce9a5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440115} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcee5b74-6097-5de5-a2f9-1ef377001ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439517} {:answer/id #uuid "cc9ac649-f4ee-5a5e-aa1e-4df3984df146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcee5b74-6097-5de5-a2f9-1ef377001ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439517} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9513575-9539-55dd-8564-2815f12cfbf6" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6851bbc7-80d6-5dc9-8a00-f559624fa12f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130217" :question/problem "At which points on the curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2y-2x$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $-i+j?$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-2,0)$\n- **II.** $(-2,2)$\n- **III.** $(0,0)$\n- **IV.** $(0,2)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2y-2x \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x-2y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x-2y,$ our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x-2y)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x-2y)\\,j \\\\  & =(2y-2)\\,i-(2x+2)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $-i+j,$ we must have $t\\cdot (-i+j)=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot (-i+j) & =0 \\\\ ((2y-2)\\,i-(2x+2)\\,j)\\cdot (-i+j) & =0 \\\\ -(2y-2)-(2x+2) & =0 \\\\ -2y-2x & =0 \\\\ y & =-x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2y-2x \\\\ {x}^{2}+(-x)^{2} & =2(-x)-2x \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =-4x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 2x(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- For $x=-2,$ we get $y=2,$ and the corresponding point is $(-2,2).$\n\n- For $x=0,$ we get $y=0,$ and the corresponding point is $(0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4c