ey "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440310} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0059f0f-4a6f-5caa-9dba-9936a289c5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439907} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3870f9-c0c6-5caa-b070-c262ba11e1fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0059f0f-4a6f-5caa-9dba-9936a289c5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439907} :answer-field/id #uuid "518a9fff-84eb-58e5-b9d5-a58af9766148" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d13fce5d-8bd4-547a-afec-720ff5befaa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71470" :question/problem "Given $h(x,y,z)=xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}.$ Find the points $(x,y,z)$ where $∇h(x,y,z)=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,0,-2)$\n- **II.** $(0,0,-2)$\n- **III.** $(0,0,0)$\n- **IV.** $(0,0,2)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =xy{e}^{x}+y{e}^{x}+0 \\\\  & =y(x+1){e}^{x} \\\\ {h}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}+0 \\\\  & =x{e}^{x} \\\\ {h}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy{e}^{x}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z}) \\\\  & =0+2z{e}^{z}+{z}^{2}{e}^{z} \\\\  & =z(2+z){e}^{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇h(x,y,z)=y(x+1){e}^{x}\\,i+x{e}^{x}\\,j+z(2+z){e}^{z}\\,k.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇h(x,y,z)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x+1){e}^{x}\\,i+x{e}^{x}\\,j+z(2+z){e}^{z}\\,k & =0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j+0\\text{ }k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$, $j$, and $k$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}y(x+1){e}^{x}=0 \\\\ x{e}^{x}=0 \\\\ z(2+z){e}^{z}=0\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nThe second equation gives $x=0.$ Substituting these into the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0+1){e}^{0} & =0 \\\\ y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the third equation, we get  $z=0$ or $z=-2.$\n\nTherefore, $∇h(x,y,z)=0$ at two points: $(0,0,0)$ and $(0,0,-2).$"}]}
